{
 "The Ram": "公羊",
 "21 March – 19 April": "3月21日 – 4月19日",
 "Masculine (outward, active)": "阳性（外向、主动）",
 "Courageous": "勇敢",
 "Pioneering": "开拓",
 "Direct": "直接",
 "Competitive": "好胜",
 "Spontaneous": "随性",
 "Aries is the first sign of the zodiac, and Aries people carry that first-ness in their bones. The Sun enters Aries at the spring equinox, when daylight finally overtakes the dark, and there is something of that turning point in how an Aries person meets life: a sudden push of energy, a readiness to begin before anyone has quite finished explaining the plan. Ruled by Mars and belonging to the cardinal fire signs, Aries starts things, and starts them with heat.": "白羊座是黄道带的第一个星座，白羊座的人骨子里就带着这份“第一”。太阳在春分时进入白羊座，那时白昼终于压过了黑夜，白羊座的人面对生活的方式里就有那个转折点的影子：一股突然的能量推动，一种在别人还没完全解释完计划之前就准备开始的劲头。白羊座由火星守护，属于本位火象星座，它开启事情，而且是带着热度开启的。",
 "In everyday life this looks like the friend who books the trip while everyone else is still comparing dates, who says the awkward thing in the meeting so it can finally be dealt with, who would rather try and fail than sit in the waiting room of maybe. Aries people tend to think with their bodies. They pace on phone calls, decide things on the walk home, and often feel clearer after moving than after mulling.": "在日常生活中，这表现为那个在别人还在比较日期时就订好旅行的朋友，那个在会议上说出尴尬之事好让它终于被处理的人，那个宁愿尝试然后失败、也不愿坐在“也许”的候诊室里的人。白羊座的人往往用身体思考。他们打电话时来回踱步，在回家的路上做决定，常常在活动之后比在苦思之后感觉更清晰。",
 "What is less often said is how honest this sign is. An Aries person rarely nurses a hidden grudge, because the anger, if it comes, comes out at once and then burns off. They can be genuinely startled to learn that someone is still upset a week later. Their emotional weather changes quickly, and they tend to assume yours does too.": "较少被提到的是这个星座有多诚实。白羊座的人很少暗中记恨，因为愤怒如果来了，会立刻冒出来，然后烧完。得知某人一周后还在生气，他们可能会真心吃惊。他们的情绪天气变化很快，他们往往以为你的也一样。",
 "The deeper lesson of Aries is the difference between courage and urgency. At their best, Aries people are brave on behalf of others: the first to stand up for someone being talked over, the first to try the new thing so everyone else feels safe to follow. The growth edge is learning that not every pause is a defeat, and that the second step, the third and the tenth deserve as much fire as the first.": "白羊座更深的功课，是勇气与急躁之间的区别。在最好的状态下，白羊座的人会为别人而勇敢：第一个为被打断的人站出来，第一个尝试新事物，让其他人都感到可以安心跟上。成长课题是学会不是每一次停顿都是失败，第二步、第三步和第十步与第一步一样值得投入那份火热。",
 "Aries people have a rare gift for momentum. Where others need permission, they need only a reason, and sometimes not even that. They are direct in a way that saves everyone time: you usually know where you stand with an Aries, and their yes means yes. Many have a physical bravery and an emotional one too, the willingness to be a beginner in public, to ask for what they want, to run first into the cold sea. They bounce back from setbacks quickly, treating a closed door as information rather than a verdict. Their enthusiasm is contagious, and they are often at their most generous when championing someone else's cause, fighting for a friend with more fire than they would ever spend on themselves.": "白羊座的人有一种罕见的势头天赋。别人需要许可，他们只需要一个理由，有时甚至连理由都不需要。他们的直接能为每个人节省时间：你通常知道自己在白羊座的人那里处于什么位置，他们说“好”就是“好”。许多人既有身体上的勇敢，也有情感上的勇敢：愿意在众人面前做一个初学者，开口要自己想要的，第一个冲进冰冷的大海。他们从挫折中恢复得很快，把一扇关上的门当作信息而不是判决。他们的热情很有感染力，在为别人的事业奔走时往往最为慷慨，为朋友而战时的火力比他们为自己花的要多得多。",
 "The same speed that makes Aries people brilliant starters can leave a trail of half-finished projects and slightly bruised feelings. Impatience is the classic shadow: with queues, with slow talkers, with their own learning curve. Under pressure they may react before they have fully listened, and a sharp word can land harder than intended, especially on gentler people who do not recover as fast. Some Aries people struggle with vulnerability, treating tenderness as a kind of losing. Competition can creep into places it does not belong, from a board game to a heartfelt conversation. The growth edge is learning to count to ten, ask one more question, and trust that slowing down is not the same as giving up.": "同样的速度让白羊座的人成为出色的开创者，也可能留下一串半途而废的项目和略微受伤的感情。急躁是经典的阴影面：对排队、对说话慢的人、对自己的学习曲线都没耐心。在压力之下，他们可能在完全听完之前就做出反应，一句尖锐的话可能比本意落得更重，尤其是落在那些恢复得没那么快的温和之人身上。有些白羊座的人与脆弱相处困难，把温柔当作一种认输。竞争可能悄悄溜进不属于它的地方，从一盘桌游到一场推心置腹的谈话。成长课题是学会数到十，再多问一个问题，相信慢下来并不等于放弃。",
 "In love, Aries people tend to know quickly and say so. They are not natural game-players; if they are interested, you will probably notice, because they will make the plans, send the first message and turn up on time. Courtship with an Aries often has a dash of adventure, a spontaneous drive to the coast or an invitation to try something neither of you has done before. They are drawn to people with spark and spine, partners who will push back rather than simply agree. What an Aries partner needs most is room to be independent without that being read as distance, and a relationship that keeps some sense of play long after the early rush. Their tempers can flare, but they usually apologise as quickly as they ignite. The growth edge is staying present through the quieter seasons of love, when nothing needs conquering and the work is simply attention, patience and showing up again tomorrow.": "在爱情中，白羊座的人往往很快就知道，并且会说出来。他们天生不是玩心理游戏的人；如果他们有兴趣，你很可能会注意到，因为他们会制订计划、发出第一条消息、准时出现。与白羊座的人恋爱常常带点冒险，一次说走就走的海边自驾，或者邀请你一起尝试你们俩都没做过的事。他们被有火花、有骨气的人吸引，被那些会反驳而不只是附和的伴侣吸引。白羊座的伴侣最需要的，是拥有独立的空间而不被解读为疏远，以及一段在最初的激情过后很久依然保有玩心的关系。他们的脾气可能会爆发，但通常道歉得和点燃得一样快。成长课题是在爱情较为平静的季节里保持在场，那时没有什么需要征服，功课只是关注、耐心，以及明天再次出现。",
 "At work, Aries people shine wherever there is something to start, fix or fight for. They are often happiest launching a project, opening up a new market, leading a pitch, or stepping into a crisis that has frozen everyone else. Roles with clear goals, visible progress and a good degree of autonomy suit them far better than slow, consensus-heavy environments. They can make inspiring leaders, setting the pace by example rather than by memo. The trouble usually comes in the middle stretch, once the excitement has faded and the work becomes maintenance. Aries people benefit enormously from collaborators who love detail and follow-through, and from breaking long projects into short sprints with real finish lines. Given a challenge and trusted to run with it, they will often outrun every expectation set for them.": "在工作中，凡是有东西需要开始、修复或争取的地方，白羊座的人都会闪光。他们常常在启动一个项目、开拓一个新市场、主导一次提案，或者走进一场让其他人都僵住的危机时最快乐。目标清晰、进展看得见、有相当自主权的角色，远比缓慢、重共识的环境更适合他们。他们可以成为鼓舞人心的领导者，以身作则地定下节奏，而不是靠备忘录。麻烦通常出现在中间那一段，兴奋褪去、工作变成维护的时候。白羊座的人会从热爱细节和收尾的合作者那里受益良多，也会从把长期项目拆成有真正终点的短冲刺中受益。给他们一个挑战，并信任他们自由发挥，他们常常会超出所有为他们设定的期望。",
 "Aries energy needs somewhere to go. Movement is often the quickest route back to calm, whether that is a brisk walk, a dance around the kitchen or a bracing swim. Because this sign runs hot and fast, gentle rituals that mark an ending help too: blowing out a red candle at the close of a hard day, or writing down one thing you are proud of before bed. Keep a small piece of carnelian on your desk as a reminder to choose courage over haste.": "白羊座的能量需要一个去处。运动常常是回归平静的最快途径，无论是快走一趟、在厨房里跳舞，还是游一个让人精神一振的泳。因为这个星座又热又快，标志结束的温和仪式也会有帮助：在艰难的一天结束时吹灭一支红色蜡烛，或者睡前写下一件你引以为傲的事。在桌上放一小块红玉髓，提醒自己选择勇气而不是匆忙。",
 "As a fire sign, Aries tends to feel an easy warmth with Leo and Sagittarius, who share its appetite for life and rarely take its bluntness personally. Air signs such as Gemini, Libra and Aquarius can fan the flame with ideas and conversation, and Libra in particular, as the opposite sign, often offers the balance Aries is quietly seeking. Earth and water signs can feel slower or more cautious, which may create friction at first, yet they frequently bring the steadiness and depth that help Aries grow. Any pairing can thrive; what matters most is respect for each other's pace.": "作为火象星座，白羊座往往与狮子座和射手座感到轻松的温暖，它们与白羊座一样热爱生活，也很少把它的直率往心里去。双子座、天秤座和水瓶座这样的风象星座能用想法和交谈为火焰扇风，尤其是作为对宫星座的天秤座，常常提供白羊座暗中寻求的平衡。土象和水象星座可能显得更慢或更谨慎，一开始可能产生摩擦，但它们常常带来帮助白羊座成长的稳定与深度。任何组合都能兴旺；最重要的是尊重彼此的节奏。",
 "The Bull": "公牛",
 "20 April – 20 May": "4月20日 – 5月20日",
 "Feminine (inward, receptive)": "阴性（内向、接纳）",
 "Steadfast": "坚定",
 "Sensual": "感性",
 "Practical": "务实",
 "Determined": "有决心",
 "Taurus people live close to the senses. They notice the weight of a good mug, the smell of rain on warm pavement, the exact moment the bread is ready. Ruled by Venus and belonging to the fixed earth signs, Taurus arrives in the full bloom of spring in the northern hemisphere, when whatever the Aries spark began has rooted and is now putting out leaves. That is the Taurus gift: to take something alive and help it last.": "金牛座的人活得贴近感官。他们注意到一只好杯子的分量、雨水落在温热路面上的气味、面包恰好烤好的那一刻。金牛座由金星守护，属于固定土象星座，在北半球春意最盛时到来，那时白羊座的火花所开启的一切已经扎根，正在长出叶子。这就是金牛座的天赋：把有生命的东西接过来，帮助它长久。",
 "Where other signs chase novelty, Taurus people tend to build. They often keep the same friends for decades, return to the same café, and know precisely how they like their tea. To an outsider this can look like stubbornness, and sometimes it is. But underneath sits a sincere philosophy: that pleasure, security and love are not luxuries but foundations, and that a good life is made from small things done well, again and again.": "其他星座追逐新鲜，金牛座的人则往往去建造。他们常常几十年都和同一群朋友来往，回到同一家咖啡馆，确切地知道自己喜欢怎样的茶。在外人看来，这可能像固执，有时也确实是。但底下有一种真诚的生活哲学：愉悦、安全感和爱不是奢侈品而是根基，美好的生活是由一遍又一遍做好的小事构成的。",
 "Taurus people are frequently calmer on the surface than they are inside. They take their time to process, and they do not like to be rushed into feelings or decisions. Once they have decided, though, they are remarkably steady, the person you call when everything is falling apart because they will simply come over, put the kettle on and stay.": "金牛座的人常常表面比内心更平静。他们需要时间来消化，不喜欢被催着产生感受或做出决定。不过一旦决定了，他们就非常稳定，是当一切都分崩离析时你会打电话找的那个人，因为他们会直接过来，烧上一壶水，然后留下来。",
 "There is often an artist in Taurus, whether that shows up as music, cooking, gardening, textiles or simply an eye for arranging a room. Venus gives this sign a feel for beauty that is tactile rather than theoretical. The growth edge for Taurus is change itself. Life will insist on moving, and the work is to learn that letting go of one form of security can make space for a deeper one, and that roots can travel.": "金牛座身上常常住着一位艺术家，无论它表现为音乐、烹饪、园艺、织物，还是只是一双会布置房间的眼睛。金星给了这个星座一种触感上而非理论上的美感。金牛座的成长课题是改变本身。生活会坚持向前移动，功课是学会放下一种形式的安全感，可以为一种更深的安全感腾出空间，而根也是可以迁移的。",
 "Taurus people offer a kind of reliability that is increasingly rare. They do what they said they would do, they remember how you take your coffee, and they are not swept away by every passing trend. Their patience is a genuine power: they can work at something for years, letting skill and value build up quietly. Many have a gift for making people feel physically at ease, with good food, soft lighting and an unhurried welcome. They tend to have sound instincts about what is worth investing time and care in. Loyal, sensual, practical and often very funny in a dry, understated way, a Taurus friend is the sort who makes ordinary days feel good.": "金牛座的人提供一种越来越罕见的可靠。他们说到做到，记得你喝咖啡的习惯，也不会被每一阵潮流卷走。他们的耐心是一种真正的力量：他们能为一件事努力好多年，让技能和价值悄悄积累。许多人有一种让人在身体上感到自在的天赋，用美食、柔和的灯光和不慌不忙的欢迎。他们对什么值得投入时间和心思往往有可靠的直觉。忠诚、感性、务实，常常还带着一种干巴巴、不动声色的幽默，金牛座的朋友是那种让平凡日子都感觉美好的人。",
 "The fixed nature of Taurus can harden into resistance. When change is proposed, a Taurus person may dig in out of habit rather than conviction, refusing to budge long after the original reason has gone. Comfort can become a hiding place, and the familiar can be chosen over the fulfilling simply because it feels safer. Some Taurus people struggle to voice anger, letting resentment build quietly until it erupts in a way that surprises everyone, including themselves. Possessiveness, of people or of plans, is another shadow to watch. The constructive path is to practise small, voluntary changes, to say what bothers you while it is still small, and to remember that flexibility is a form of strength.": "金牛座的固定特质可能硬化成抗拒。当有人提出改变时，金牛座的人可能出于习惯而不是信念坚守不动，在最初的理由早已消失之后很久仍然不肯让步。舒适可能变成一个藏身之处，熟悉的东西可能仅仅因为感觉更安全而被选中，胜过那些令人满足的东西。有些金牛座的人很难表达愤怒，让怨恨悄悄积累，直到以一种让所有人、包括他们自己都吃惊的方式爆发。对人或对计划的占有欲是另一个需要留意的阴影面。建设性的道路是练习小小的、自愿的改变，在烦恼还小时就说出来，并记住灵活也是一种力量。",
 "Taurus people love slowly and mean it. They are rarely in a hurry to define things, preferring to let trust grow at its own pace, but once committed they are devoted, affectionate and physically warm. Romance for a Taurus is concrete: a meal cooked properly, a hand resting on yours, a gift chosen because it will actually be used. They show love through presence and care more than grand declarations, and they notice whether a partner does the same. Consistency matters enormously; flakiness or mixed signals can quietly end their interest. A Taurus partner needs to feel safe, valued and appreciated for the steady things they do. The growth edge in love is allowing a relationship to evolve, and recognising that a partner's need for change is not a threat to the bond but part of what keeps it alive.": "金牛座的人爱得慢，而且是认真的。他们很少急于给关系下定义，更愿意让信任按自己的节奏生长，但一旦投入，他们就全心全意、充满爱意、身体上很温暖。对金牛座来说，浪漫是具体的：一顿好好做的饭、一只搭在你手上的手、一份因为真的会被用上而挑选的礼物。他们更多通过陪伴和照顾来表达爱，而不是宏大的宣言，他们也会注意伴侣是否同样如此。始终如一极其重要；忽冷忽热或混杂的信号可能悄悄终结他们的兴趣。金牛座的伴侣需要感到安全、被珍视，他们所做的那些稳定的事需要被欣赏。爱情中的成长课题是允许一段关系演变，并认识到伴侣对改变的需要不是对这份羁绊的威胁，而是让它保持鲜活的一部分。",
 "At work, Taurus people are builders and keepers. They thrive where patience is rewarded and quality matters more than speed: craft, design, food, horticulture, finance, property, music, or any role that turns raw material into something lasting. Colleagues tend to trust them because they are calm under pressure and steady through long projects. They prefer clear expectations, a pleasant environment and the freedom to work at their own rhythm, and they do not respond well to constant reorganisation or being hurried for the sake of it. Once they have mastered a method, they can be reluctant to drop it, which is worth watching in fast-moving fields. Given time and trust, a Taurus person often becomes the backbone of a team, quietly holding the standards everyone else relies on.": "在工作中，金牛座的人是建造者和守护者。他们在耐心会得到回报、质量比速度更重要的地方如鱼得水：手工艺、设计、食品、园艺、金融、房地产、音乐，或者任何把原材料变成持久之物的角色。同事们往往信任他们，因为他们在压力下很冷静，在漫长的项目中很稳定。他们更喜欢清晰的期望、宜人的环境以及按自己节奏工作的自由，对不断的重组或为了快而被催促反应不佳。一旦掌握了一种方法，他们可能不愿放弃，这在快速变化的领域里值得留意。给他们时间和信任，金牛座的人常常会成为一个团队的脊梁，安静地守住所有人都依赖的标准。",
 "Taurus self-care is unashamedly sensory. A long bath, fresh flowers on the table, a slow meal eaten without a screen, bare feet on grass or sand: for this sign these are not indulgences but ways of coming home to the body. Time in a garden or tending houseplants can be especially soothing. When life feels unsettled, try a simple grounding ritual: hold a piece of rose quartz or green aventurine, breathe slowly, and name five things you can feel, smell or hear right now.": "金牛座的自我照顾毫不掩饰地诉诸感官。一个长长的泡澡、桌上的鲜花、一顿不看屏幕慢慢吃完的饭、赤脚踩在草地或沙滩上：对这个星座来说，这些不是放纵，而是回到身体的方式。在花园里待一会儿或照料室内植物会格外抚慰人心。当生活感觉不安定时，试试一个简单的接地仪式：握一颗粉晶或一块东陵玉，慢慢呼吸，说出此刻你能感觉到、闻到或听到的五样东西。",
 "Taurus usually feels at home with fellow earth signs, Virgo and Capricorn, who share its practical values and appreciation of steadiness. Water signs such as Cancer and Pisces often bring the emotional depth and tenderness Taurus quietly craves, and the combination can be very nurturing. Scorpio, its opposite sign, can be intensely magnetic, a pull between comfort and transformation. Fire and air signs may feel restless or unpredictable to Taurus at first, yet they can also coax it out of routine and into new experiences. With patience on both sides, any match can find common ground.": "金牛座通常与同为土象的处女座和摩羯座感到自在，它们共享金牛座务实的价值观和对稳定的欣赏。巨蟹座和双鱼座这样的水象星座常常带来金牛座暗中渴望的情感深度与温柔，这种组合可以非常滋养人。作为对宫星座的天蝎座可能有强烈的吸引力，是舒适与转化之间的一股拉力。火象和风象星座一开始可能让金牛座觉得躁动或难以预料，但它们也能哄着金牛座走出日常、进入新的体验。只要双方都有耐心，任何组合都能找到共同点。",
 "The Twins": "双子",
 "21 May – 20 June": "5月21日 – 6月20日",
 "Adaptable": "适应力强",
 "Communicative": "善于沟通",
 "Versatile": "多才多艺",
 "Sociable": "合群",
 "Gemini people are collectors of the world. Conversations, facts, jokes, half-overheard stories on the bus, the name of that plant, the way a word shifts meaning from one language to another: everything is potentially interesting, and most of it is. Ruled by Mercury, the messenger, and belonging to the mutable air signs, Gemini arrives as spring tips into summer, when the hedgerows are busy with birds and everything seems to be talking at once.": "双子座的人是这个世界的收集者。交谈、事实、笑话、在公交车上偶然听到一半的故事、那种植物的名字、一个词在不同语言之间意思的变化：一切都可能很有趣，而且大多数确实如此。双子座由信使水星守护，属于变动风象星座，在春天转入夏天时到来，那时树篱里满是鸟儿，一切仿佛都在同时说话。",
 "The usual story about Gemini is that they are fickle or two-faced, and it misses the point. What Gemini people actually have is range. They can hold two ideas in mind at the same time and enjoy the tension between them. They change their minds because they keep learning, and they often see several sides of a question long before anyone else has noticed there was more than one. That flexibility makes them excellent company, bridge-builders and translators, between people as much as between languages.": "关于双子座的常见说法是他们善变或两面派，这完全没说到点子上。双子座的人真正拥有的是广度。他们能同时在脑中容纳两个想法，并享受它们之间的张力。他们改变主意是因为他们一直在学习，他们常常在别人还没注意到一个问题不止一面之前，就已经看到了它的好几面。这份灵活让他们成为极好的伙伴、桥梁搭建者和翻译者，在人与人之间也在语言与语言之间。",
 "In daily life, a Gemini person might have six tabs open, three books on the go and a group chat that never quite goes quiet. They often think best out loud, so talking a problem through is not idle chatter but the way their mind works. Boredom can feel almost physical to them, and they tend to wilt in routines that offer nothing new.": "在日常生活中，一个双子座的人可能开着六个网页标签，同时在读三本书，还有一个从来不会真正安静下来的群聊。他们常常在大声说出来时思考得最好，所以把一个问题聊透并不是闲聊，而是他们头脑运作的方式。无聊对他们来说几乎是身体上的感受，在没有任何新鲜感的日常里，他们往往会蔫下去。",
 "Beneath the quickness, Gemini people are frequently more sensitive than they appear, using humour and curiosity to keep heavier feelings at a manageable distance. The growth edge for this sign is depth: choosing a few things to follow all the way down, and learning that staying with one feeling, one person or one question can be as fascinating as moving on to the next.": "在敏捷之下，双子座的人常常比看起来更敏感，用幽默和好奇把更沉重的感受保持在可以应付的距离之外。这个星座的成长课题是深度：选择几样东西一路追到底，并学会与一种感受、一个人或一个问题待在一起，可以和转向下一个一样迷人。",
 "Gemini people are wonderfully quick. They pick up new skills fast, read a room in seconds and can talk to almost anyone, from a shy child to a sceptical stranger at a party. Their curiosity is genuine rather than performative, and it makes the people around them feel interesting. They are natural explainers, able to take a complicated idea and make it light and clear. Adaptable and witty, they cope with changing plans better than most and often find the funny side of a difficult day. Many Gemini people are gifted writers, teachers and connectors, the friend who always seems to know someone who can help.": "双子座的人反应快得惊人。他们学新技能很快，几秒钟就能读懂一个房间，几乎能和任何人聊天，从一个害羞的孩子到派对上一个心存怀疑的陌生人。他们的好奇是真诚的而不是表演的，这让身边的人感到自己很有趣。他们是天生的解释者，能把一个复杂的想法变得轻盈而清晰。适应力强、机智风趣，他们比大多数人更能应付变化的计划，常常能在艰难的一天里找到有趣的一面。许多双子座的人是天赋出众的写作者、老师和连接者，是那个似乎总认识能帮上忙的人的朋友。",
 "The restlessness that keeps Gemini lively can also scatter it. Too many projects, too many messages, too many possibilities, and nothing quite gets finished. Some Gemini people talk around a feeling rather than through it, using analysis or a clever line to dodge discomfort. Others can appear inconsistent, saying yes enthusiastically and then changing course when something more interesting appears, which can leave friends unsure where they stand. Nervous energy may show up as overthinking or difficulty switching off at night. The constructive path is to choose fewer commitments and honour them, to notice when chatter is covering a deeper need, and to protect real quiet time for the mind to settle.": "让双子座保持活力的躁动也可能让它分散。太多的项目、太多的消息、太多的可能性，结果什么都没有真正完成。有些双子座的人绕着一种感受说话而不是穿过它，用分析或一句妙语来躲避不适。另一些人可能显得前后不一，热情地答应，然后在出现更有趣的东西时改变方向，这可能让朋友们不确定自己处在什么位置。紧张的能量可能表现为想太多，或者晚上很难关机。建设性的道路是选择更少的承诺并兑现它们，留意喋喋不休何时在掩盖一份更深的需要，并保护真正安静的时间，让头脑沉淀下来。",
 "For Gemini people, attraction usually starts in the mind. A clever reply, a shared joke, a conversation that runs until the café closes: these are the things that make a Gemini lean in. They tend to flirt with words and ideas, and they need a partner who can keep up, surprise them and, crucially, be a friend as well as a lover. Variety matters; a relationship that becomes predictable can feel stifling, so new places, new games and new topics keep the spark alive. Gemini partners are often playful, affectionate and generous with attention, though they may need encouragement to talk about feelings directly rather than skating over them. The growth edge in love is letting someone see the less polished, less entertaining side of you, and trusting that the relationship can hold your moods and silences as well as your sparkle.": "对双子座的人来说，吸引通常从头脑开始。一句聪明的回复、一个共享的笑话、一场聊到咖啡馆打烊的谈话：这些才是让双子座凑近的东西。他们往往用话语和想法调情，他们需要一个能跟得上、能给他们惊喜、而且关键是既是恋人也是朋友的伴侣。多样性很重要；一段变得可以预测的关系可能让人窒息，所以新的地方、新的游戏和新的话题能让火花保持鲜活。双子座的伴侣常常俏皮、充满爱意、慷慨地给予关注，不过他们可能需要鼓励才能直接谈论感受，而不是一笔带过。爱情中的成长课题是让某个人看到你不那么光鲜、不那么有趣的一面，并相信这段关系能容纳你的情绪和沉默，就像它容纳你的闪光一样。",
 "Gemini people thrive in work that is varied, social and mentally lively. Writing, journalism, teaching, marketing, sales, translation, media, events and anything involving information or communication tend to suit them, as do roles that let them juggle several projects rather than grind through one. They are often brilliant at the start of things, spotting connections, generating ideas and bringing the right people together. Long, repetitive tasks can drain them quickly, and they may procrastinate on anything that feels dull. Pairing them with a steady finisher, or building variety into the working week, can make a big difference. Gemini people also tend to learn on the job remarkably fast, so changing careers or adding new skills later in life often feels natural to them rather than daunting.": "双子座的人在多样、社交性强、思维活跃的工作中如鱼得水。写作、新闻、教学、市场营销、销售、翻译、媒体、活动策划，以及任何涉及信息或沟通的工作往往适合他们，那些让他们同时兼顾几个项目而不是埋头苦干一个的角色也一样。他们常常在事情开始时表现出色，发现联系、产生想法、把对的人聚在一起。漫长而重复的任务可能很快耗尽他们，他们也可能拖延任何感觉乏味的事。让他们与一个稳定的收尾者搭档，或者在工作周中安排多样的内容，能带来很大的不同。双子座的人在工作中学习得也非常快，所以在人生后期转换职业或增加新技能，对他们来说常常感觉很自然而不是令人畏惧。",
 "Gemini minds benefit from a gentle off switch. A short evening walk without headphones, journalling to empty the thoughts onto paper, or reading something purely for pleasure can help settle a busy head. Breathwork suits this air sign especially well; even a few slow breaths, with the exhale longer than the inhale, can shift the mood. On the new moon, try writing down three things you want to learn this month, then cross one out, leaving room to go deeper with the other two.": "双子座的头脑需要一个温和的关机键。晚上不戴耳机散一小段步、写日记把思绪倒在纸上，或者纯粹为了乐趣读点东西，能帮助忙碌的脑袋安定下来。呼吸练习格外适合这个风象星座；哪怕只是几次缓慢的呼吸，让呼气比吸气更长，都能转换情绪。在新月时，试着写下这个月想学的三样东西，然后划掉一样，留出空间对另外两样学得更深。",
 "Gemini tends to feel immediately at ease with fellow air signs, Libra and Aquarius, who share its love of ideas and conversation. Fire signs such as Aries and Leo often bring warmth and excitement that Gemini finds energising, and Sagittarius, its opposite sign, can be a lively match of curious minds pulling in slightly different directions. Earth signs may seem steady but serious, while water signs can feel emotionally intense to an airy Gemini; these pairings ask for patience and translation, yet they often offer exactly the grounding or depth Gemini has been missing.": "双子座往往与同为风象的天秤座和水瓶座一见如故，它们共享双子座对想法和交谈的热爱。白羊座和狮子座这样的火象星座常常带来双子座觉得充满活力的温暖与兴奋，作为对宫星座的射手座，可能是一场活泼的组合，两颗好奇的头脑朝着略微不同的方向拉扯。土象星座可能显得稳重却严肃，而水象星座可能让风一般的双子座觉得情感上太强烈；这些组合需要耐心和相互翻译，但它们常常恰好提供双子座一直缺少的接地或深度。",
 "The Crab": "螃蟹",
 "21 June – 22 July": "6月21日 – 7月22日",
 "the Moon": "月亮",
 "Nurturing": "善于照顾",
 "Tender": "温柔",
 "Imaginative": "富于想象",
 "Home-loving": "恋家",
 "Cancer people know how to make a place feel like home. They remember birthdays, notice when someone has gone quiet, and keep a cupboard stocked with whatever a visitor might need. Ruled by the Moon and belonging to the cardinal water signs, Cancer begins at the summer solstice, the longest day of the year, when the light is at its fullest and, from that moment, slowly begins to turn. There is something of that tender turning point in Cancer: a sign that holds the fullness of feeling, and knows it will change.": "巨蟹座的人懂得如何让一个地方有家的感觉。他们记得生日，注意到有人变得沉默，橱柜里总备着访客可能需要的东西。巨蟹座由月亮守护，属于本位水象星座，始于夏至，一年中白昼最长的一天，那时光线最为充沛，而从那一刻起，它便开始慢慢转向。巨蟹座身上有那个温柔转折点的影子：一个承载着满满感受、也知道它们会改变的星座。",
 "The crab is a perfect emblem. Hard shell, soft interior, and a sideways way of approaching things that is often wiser than marching straight in. Cancer people can seem reserved or guarded with strangers, but once trust is established they are among the warmest, funniest and most protective friends anyone could have. Their humour, often gently teasing, is one of the sign's best-kept secrets.": "螃蟹是一个完美的象征。坚硬的外壳、柔软的内里，以及一种横着靠近事物的方式，常常比直直地走进去更明智。巨蟹座的人在陌生人面前可能显得拘谨或戒备，但一旦建立了信任，他们就是任何人所能拥有的最温暖、最有趣、最有保护欲的朋友之一。他们常常带着温和调侃的幽默，是这个星座保守得最好的秘密之一。",
 "Being cardinal, Cancer is more active than it is usually given credit for. These are people who start families of every kind: friendship groups, community projects, small businesses that feel like a second home. They lead through care, and they will fight fiercely for the people and places they love.": "作为本位星座，巨蟹座比人们通常认为的更主动。这些人会建立各种形式的家：朋友圈、社区项目、感觉像第二个家的小生意。他们通过关怀来领导，他们会为所爱的人和地方激烈地战斗。",
 "Like the Moon, Cancer moods wax and wane, and they often feel the emotional undercurrent of a room before anyone has spoken. That sensitivity is a gift, but it can also make them absorb other people's worries as if they were their own. The growth edge for Cancer is learning to nurture themselves as faithfully as they nurture others, and to open the shell on purpose rather than only when it feels completely safe.": "像月亮一样，巨蟹座的情绪有盈有亏，他们常常在任何人开口之前就感觉到房间里的情感暗流。这份敏感是一份礼物，但它也可能让他们把别人的忧虑吸收成自己的。巨蟹座的成长课题是学会像照顾别人一样忠实地照顾自己，并有意识地打开外壳，而不只是在感到完全安全时才打开。",
 "Cancer people have deep emotional intelligence. They sense what others need, often before it has been said, and respond with practical kindness: a meal, a message, a spare bed. Their loyalty is steadfast, and they tend to keep relationships going across years and distances. They have long memories for the good things people have done, and they treasure shared history, old photos and family stories, whatever family means to them. Intuitive and imaginative, many Cancer people are gifted at creating atmosphere, hosting and making others feel looked after. When someone they love is threatened, the gentle crab reveals real courage and a fierce protective streak.": "巨蟹座的人有很深的情商。他们能感知别人需要什么，常常在对方说出口之前，并以实际的善意回应：一顿饭、一条消息、一张空床。他们的忠诚坚定不移，往往能跨越岁月和距离维系关系。他们对别人做过的好事记得很久，珍视共同的历史、老照片和家族故事，无论家对他们意味着什么。富于直觉和想象，许多巨蟹座的人擅长营造氛围、招待客人、让别人感到被照顾。当他们所爱的人受到威胁时，温柔的螃蟹会展现出真正的勇气和凶猛的保护欲。",
 "Because Cancer feels so much, it can also be easily hurt, and the instinct is to retreat into the shell rather than say what has wounded it. That can lead to sulking, indirect hints or a hope that others will simply guess. Moodiness is the classic shadow, along with a tendency to hold on to old slights for longer than is helpful. Some Cancer people care for others so thoroughly that they lose track of their own needs, then feel quietly resentful when the care is not returned. Nostalgia can tip into living in the past. The constructive path is direct, gentle honesty about feelings, firm boundaries, and receiving care as readily as giving it.": "因为巨蟹座感受如此之多，它也很容易受伤，而它的本能是缩回壳里，而不是说出是什么伤了它。这可能导致生闷气、拐弯抹角的暗示，或者希望别人能自己猜到。情绪化是经典的阴影面，还有一种把旧日的怠慢抓得比有益的时间更久的倾向。有些巨蟹座的人如此周到地照顾别人，以至于忘了自己的需要，然后在关心没有得到回报时暗暗怨恨。怀旧可能滑向活在过去。建设性的道路是直接而温和地诚实表达感受，设定坚定的界限，像给予关怀一样乐于接受关怀。",
 "Cancer people love with their whole heart, but they rarely hand it over all at once. Early on they may test the waters, watching how a partner treats waiters, friends and family, and whether they keep their word. Once safe, Cancer becomes deeply affectionate, attentive and romantic in a homely way: cooking your favourite dish, remembering the little thing you mentioned months ago, building rituals that belong only to the two of you. Emotional security is the heart of the matter; reassurance, consistency and kindness go a long way. Partners should know that a Cancer person's silence usually signals hurt rather than indifference. The growth edge in love is speaking feelings plainly instead of waiting to be understood, and trusting that a relationship can survive conflict, even grow closer through it, rather than needing to be protected from every storm.": "巨蟹座的人全心全意地去爱，但他们很少一下子就把心交出去。早期他们可能会试探，观察伴侣如何对待服务员、朋友和家人，以及是否信守承诺。一旦感到安全，巨蟹座就会变得深情、体贴，以一种居家的方式浪漫：做你最爱的菜，记得你几个月前提过的小事，建立只属于你们两人的仪式。情感上的安全感是问题的核心；安慰、始终如一和善意能起很大的作用。伴侣应该知道，巨蟹座的人沉默通常意味着受伤而不是漠不关心。爱情中的成长课题是直白地说出感受，而不是等着被理解，并相信一段关系能挺过冲突，甚至因此更加亲近，而不需要被保护起来免受每一场风暴。",
 "Cancer people often do their best work when they care about the people involved. Teaching, hospitality, food, interior design, property, history and heritage, counselling and community work can all suit them, as can running a small business with a family feel. They tend to be loyal employees and protective managers, the kind who notice when a colleague is struggling and quietly cover for them. Cardinal energy gives them more ambition than they sometimes admit, and they can be shrewd, careful with resources and good at reading what customers really want. They work less well in cold, cut-throat cultures where feelings are dismissed. A Cancer person who feels emotionally safe at work becomes a powerful, intuitive asset and is often the one holding the whole team together.": "巨蟹座的人常常在他们在乎所涉及之人时做出最好的工作。教学、餐饮旅宿、食品、室内设计、房地产、历史与遗产、心理咨询和社区工作都可能适合他们，经营一家有家庭氛围的小生意也是。他们往往是忠诚的员工和有保护欲的管理者，会注意到同事何时在挣扎，并悄悄替对方顶上。本位星座的能量给了他们比他们有时承认的更多的抱负，他们可以精明、谨慎地对待资源，善于读懂顾客真正想要什么。在感受被轻视的冷漠、你死我活的文化中，他们工作得不太好。一个在工作中感到情感安全的巨蟹座的人，会成为一份强大而富于直觉的资产，常常是那个把整个团队凝聚在一起的人。",
 "Cancer recharges through water, comfort and the Moon itself. A warm bath with salts, time by the sea or a river, or simply curling up at home with a familiar film can soothe an overstretched heart. Tracking how you feel through the lunar month may reveal useful patterns. Try a full moon ritual of release: write down a worry you have been carrying for someone else, hold a moonstone for a few breaths, then gently tear the paper and let it go.": "巨蟹座通过水、舒适和月亮本身来恢复元气。一个加了浴盐的温水澡、在海边或河边的时光，或者只是蜷在家里看一部熟悉的电影，能抚慰一颗过度劳累的心。追踪自己在一个月亮周期中的感受，可能会发现有用的规律。试试一个满月释放仪式：写下一件你一直在替别人背负的忧虑，握着一块月光石呼吸几次，然后轻轻撕掉那张纸，放下它。",
 "Cancer tends to feel understood by fellow water signs, Scorpio and Pisces, who share its emotional depth and intuition. Earth signs such as Taurus and Virgo often provide the stability and practical care Cancer longs for, and Capricorn, its opposite sign, can create a strong partnership of home and ambition. Fire signs may seem bold and exciting but sometimes too blunt for Cancer's sensitivity, while air signs can feel a little detached. Even so, these pairings can teach Cancer confidence and perspective when both people stay kind about their differences.": "巨蟹座往往觉得被同为水象的天蝎座和双鱼座所理解，它们共享巨蟹座的情感深度和直觉。金牛座和处女座这样的土象星座常常提供巨蟹座渴望的稳定和实际的照顾，作为对宫星座的摩羯座，可以组成一段家庭与抱负的有力伙伴关系。火象星座可能显得大胆而令人兴奋，但有时对巨蟹座的敏感来说太直接了，而风象星座可能显得有点疏离。即便如此，只要双方都善意地对待彼此的差异，这些组合也能教会巨蟹座自信和视角。",
 "The Lion": "狮子",
 "23 July – 22 August": "7月23日 – 8月22日",
 "the Sun": "太阳",
 "Warm-hearted": "热心",
 "Expressive": "富于表现力",
 "Leo people bring warmth into a room the way the Sun brings warmth into a day. Ruled by the Sun itself and belonging to the fixed fire signs, Leo arrives in the height of summer, when the evenings are long and people gather outdoors. That sense of gathering is key. This sign wants life to be lived generously, with colour, laughter and a circle of friends, and Leo people are often the ones who make it happen.": "狮子座的人为一个房间带来温暖，就像太阳为一天带来温暖。狮子座由太阳本身守护，属于固定火象星座，在盛夏到来，那时傍晚很长，人们聚在户外。那种相聚的感觉是关键。这个星座希望生活被慷慨地活着，带着色彩、笑声和一圈朋友，而狮子座的人常常就是让它发生的那些人。",
 "It is easy to reduce Leo to vanity or love of the spotlight, but that misses its heart. What drives Leo is a deep wish to create, to express something real and to be recognised for it. Leo people want to matter, and they want those they love to feel that they matter too. They are the friend who hypes up your new haircut, throws the surprise party and gives the toast that makes everyone cry.": "人们很容易把狮子座简化为虚荣或爱出风头，但这错过了它的心。驱动狮子座的，是一种深深的愿望：去创造，去表达某种真实的东西，并因此而被认可。狮子座的人想要重要，也想让他们所爱的人感到自己重要。他们是那个为你的新发型大声叫好、办惊喜派对、致辞让所有人都哭了的朋友。",
 "Being fixed, Leo has staying power. Its loyalty is legendary, and once a Leo person has decided you are one of theirs, they will defend you fiercely. Pride is part of the package, yes, but so is dignity, a sense that life should be met with an open heart and a straight back.": "作为固定星座，狮子座有持久力。它的忠诚是传奇性的，一旦一个狮子座的人认定你是自己人，他们就会激烈地捍卫你。骄傲是其中的一部分，没错，但尊严也是，一种认为生活应该以敞开的心和挺直的脊梁去面对的感觉。",
 "Behind the confident roar, many Leo people carry a tender fear of being overlooked or not quite enough. Praise matters to them more than they may admit, and criticism can sting deeply. The growth edge for Leo is learning to shine from the inside rather than waiting for applause, and discovering that the most radiant thing about them is not the performance but the generosity of their heart.": "在自信的咆哮背后，许多狮子座的人怀着一种温柔的恐惧，害怕被忽视，或者不够好。赞美对他们的重要性比他们可能承认的更大，批评也可能深深刺痛他们。狮子座的成长课题是学会从内在发光，而不是等待掌声，并发现他们身上最耀眼的东西不是表演，而是他们那颗心的慷慨。",
 "Leo people are generous in spirit. They give compliments freely, celebrate other people's wins and bring a sense of occasion to ordinary days. Their confidence is catching, helping shyer friends take risks they would never take alone. Creative, playful and often naturally theatrical, they know how to make an experience memorable. Leo loyalty runs deep, and they tend to show up for the people they love with warmth and practical support. Many have a strong moral sense and a real dislike of meanness, standing up for what is fair. At their best, Leo people lead not through force but through encouragement, making everyone around them feel a little braver.": "狮子座的人精神上很慷慨。他们慷慨地给予赞美，庆祝别人的成功，为平凡的日子带来一种仪式感。他们的自信会感染人，帮助更害羞的朋友去冒那些他们独自永远不会冒的险。富有创意、爱玩，常常天生带着戏剧感，他们知道如何让一次经历令人难忘。狮子座的忠诚很深，他们往往以温暖和实际的支持出现在所爱之人身边。许多人有强烈的道德感，真心厌恶刻薄，会为公平挺身而出。在最好的状态下，狮子座的人不是靠强力而是靠鼓励来领导，让身边的每个人都变得更勇敢一点。",
 "The Leo need for recognition can tip into needing to be the centre of attention, and friends may feel overshadowed or cast as the audience. Pride can make it hard to admit a mistake or ask for help, and a wounded Leo may become dramatic or withdraw into hurt dignity. Being fixed, they can be stubborn once they have taken a position, especially if backing down feels like losing face. Some Leo people lean heavily on outside praise, feeling flat or anxious when it is missing. The constructive path is to cultivate self-worth that does not depend on applause, to practise listening as generously as they perform, and to let others shine too.": "狮子座对认可的需要可能滑向需要成为关注的中心，朋友们可能感到被盖过，或者被分配成观众。骄傲可能让他们难以承认错误或寻求帮助，一个受伤的狮子座可能变得戏剧化，或者退缩进受伤的尊严里。作为固定星座，一旦表明了立场，他们可能很固执，尤其是在让步感觉像丢面子的时候。有些狮子座的人严重依赖外界的赞美，在缺少它时感到失落或焦虑。建设性的道路是培养一种不依赖掌声的自我价值，练习像表演一样慷慨地倾听，并让别人也发光。",
 "Leo people love in full colour. They tend to be romantic, affectionate and openly proud of their partner, the type to plan a beautiful birthday, write a heartfelt card or simply tell the world how lucky they feel. Courtship with a Leo can feel like being invited onto a stage: warm, playful and a little dramatic. What they ask in return is admiration and loyalty; they want to feel chosen, appreciated and taken seriously. Indifference or public embarrassment can hurt a Leo deeply. They are often wonderfully generous and protective partners, though they may need reminding that love is not a performance to be won. The growth edge in love is vulnerability: showing the uncertain, unpolished parts of themselves and trusting they will still be adored, and letting a partner take the lead, and the limelight, some of the time.": "狮子座的人以全彩去爱。他们往往浪漫、深情，公开地为伴侣感到骄傲，是那种会策划一个美丽的生日、写一张真情流露的卡片，或者只是告诉全世界自己有多幸运的人。与狮子座的人恋爱可能感觉像被邀请走上一个舞台：温暖、俏皮，还有点戏剧化。他们所要求的回报是欣赏和忠诚；他们想感到被选择、被欣赏、被认真对待。冷漠或当众出丑可能深深伤害一个狮子座。他们常常是非常慷慨、有保护欲的伴侣，不过他们可能需要被提醒，爱不是一场要赢的表演。爱情中的成长课题是脆弱：展露自己不确定、不光鲜的部分，相信自己依然会被爱慕，并时不时让伴侣带头，也让对方站在聚光灯下。",
 "Leo people flourish in work that lets them create, lead or be seen. The arts, performance, design, teaching, events, marketing, management, entrepreneurship and any role with a public face can suit them well. They bring energy, vision and a sense of pride to what they do, and they often lift team morale simply by turning up enthusiastic. Recognition is a powerful motivator; a Leo who feels unappreciated may lose heart quickly, so they do best with managers who give genuine feedback and credit. They tend to dislike being micromanaged or tucked away out of sight. As leaders, Leo people at their best are warm and inspiring, championing their team's achievements, though they benefit from learning to delegate gracefully and to hear constructive criticism without taking it as a personal wound.": "狮子座的人在能让他们创造、领导或被看见的工作中蓬勃发展。艺术、表演、设计、教学、活动策划、市场营销、管理、创业，以及任何需要面向公众的角色，都可能很适合他们。他们为所做的事带来能量、远见和一种自豪感，他们常常只要热情地出现就能提振团队士气。认可是强大的动力；一个感到不被欣赏的狮子座可能很快就灰心，所以他们和那些给予真诚反馈与功劳的管理者在一起时表现最好。他们往往不喜欢被事事过问，或者被藏在看不见的地方。作为领导者，最好状态下的狮子座温暖而鼓舞人心，为团队的成就喝彩，不过他们会从学会优雅地授权、学会听取建设性批评而不把它当作人身伤害中受益。",
 "Leo self-care involves play and light. Dancing to a favourite song, painting, singing loudly in the car or spending a slow afternoon in the sun can restore the Leo spirit. Creative expression done purely for joy, with no audience in mind, is especially nourishing. Try a simple morning ritual: light a gold or orange candle, place a hand on your heart and name one thing you admire about yourself, then one thing you admire about someone else. Let both feel equally true.": "狮子座的自我照顾涉及玩耍和光。随着最爱的歌跳舞、画画、在车里大声唱歌，或者在阳光下度过一个慢悠悠的下午，都能恢复狮子座的精神。纯粹为了快乐、不考虑任何观众的创作表达，格外滋养人。试试一个简单的晨间仪式：点一支金色或橙色的蜡烛，把一只手放在心口，说出一件你欣赏自己的地方，再说出一件你欣赏别人的地方。让两者感觉同样真实。",
 "Leo usually sparks easily with fellow fire signs, Aries and Sagittarius, who match its zest, warmth and appetite for adventure. Air signs such as Gemini and Libra often fan Leo's flame with wit and charm, and Aquarius, its opposite sign, can be a fascinating pairing of heart and mind, the personal and the collective. Earth signs may feel grounding but cautious, while water signs can offer a deep devotion Leo treasures, though they may want more quiet intimacy than spectacle. With mutual respect and appreciation, every combination has something to offer.": "狮子座通常很容易与同为火象的白羊座和射手座擦出火花，它们与狮子座的热情、温暖和对冒险的胃口相匹配。双子座和天秤座这样的风象星座常常用机智和魅力为狮子座的火焰扇风，作为对宫星座的水瓶座，可以是一段引人入胜的组合，关于心与脑、个人与集体。土象星座可能让人感到踏实却谨慎，而水象星座能提供狮子座珍视的深沉投入，尽管它们可能想要更多安静的亲密而不是盛大场面。只要相互尊重和欣赏，每一种组合都有它可贵之处。",
 "The Maiden": "处女",
 "23 August – 22 September": "8月23日 – 9月22日",
 "Discerning": "有辨别力",
 "Helpful": "乐于助人",
 "Analytical": "善于分析",
 "Modest": "谦逊",
 "Devoted": "全心投入",
 "Virgo people notice what others miss. The typo on the sign, the friend who is quieter than usual, the small change that would make the whole system run more smoothly: Virgo sees it and, more often than not, quietly does something about it. Ruled by Mercury and belonging to the mutable earth signs, Virgo arrives at harvest time, as summer softens into autumn and the work turns to gathering, sorting and preserving what has grown. That is the Virgo spirit: to separate the useful from the waste and to tend what matters.": "处女座的人能注意到别人错过的东西。招牌上的错别字、比平时更安静的朋友、能让整个系统运转得更顺畅的小改动：处女座看到了，而且多半会悄悄地做点什么。处女座由水星守护，属于变动土象星座，在收获时节到来，那时夏天柔化为秋天，工作转向收集、分拣和保存已经生长出来的东西。这就是处女座的精神：把有用的和无用的分开，照料重要的东西。",
 "The common caricature is a fussy perfectionist with a label maker, and while some Virgo people do love a well-organised drawer, the real point is devotion. Virgo cares about doing things properly because it cares about people, and practical help is one of its deepest forms of love. Fixing the wobbly shelf, planning the easiest route for a friend's journey, remembering exactly how you like your toast: these are Virgo love letters.": "常见的漫画形象是一个拿着标签机、吹毛求疵的完美主义者，虽然有些处女座的人确实喜欢一个整理得井井有条的抽屉，但真正的重点是投入。处女座在乎把事情做好，是因为它在乎人，实际的帮助是它最深的爱的形式之一。修好那个摇晃的架子、为朋友的旅途规划最轻松的路线、确切记得你喜欢怎样的吐司：这些都是处女座的情书。",
 "Being mutable, Virgo is more adaptable than it is given credit for. Its mind is analytical but flexible, always refining and improving, open to a better method the moment one appears. Many Virgo people have a dry, sharp wit and an appreciation for craft in every field, from bread-making to coding.": "作为变动星座，处女座比人们认为的更有适应力。它的头脑善于分析却很灵活，总在提炼和改进，一旦出现更好的方法就乐于接受。许多处女座的人有一种冷峻锋利的幽默感，以及对各个领域手艺的欣赏，从做面包到写代码。",
 "The shadow of all that noticing is that Virgo people often turn the critical eye on themselves most harshly. They may feel that they are never quite finished, never quite good enough. The growth edge for Virgo is accepting that imperfection is part of anything alive, and learning to offer themselves the same patient, practical kindness they offer everyone else.": "所有这些留意的阴影面在于，处女座的人常常把挑剔的目光最严厉地对准自己。他们可能觉得自己永远没有真正完成，永远不够好。处女座的成长课题是接受不完美是任何有生命之物的一部分，并学会给自己同样耐心而实际的善意，就像他们给每一个人的那样。",
 "Virgo people are thoughtful, capable and genuinely helpful. They pay attention to the details that make a real difference, and their work is usually careful, well researched and reliable. They tend to be modest, preferring to let results speak rather than seeking praise. Their analytical minds can untangle problems that leave others overwhelmed, breaking them down into clear, manageable steps. Many Virgo people are excellent listeners and practical advisers, the friend you call for a sensible second opinion. They have a quiet sense of humour and a strong ethical streak, wanting to be of real use in the world. Loyal and steady, they show love through small, consistent acts of service.": "处女座的人体贴、能干、真心乐于助人。他们关注那些真正能带来不同的细节，他们的工作通常细致、调研充分、可靠。他们往往谦逊，更愿意让结果说话而不是寻求赞美。他们善于分析的头脑能理清那些让别人不知所措的问题，把它们拆成清晰可控的步骤。许多处女座的人是极好的倾听者和务实的建议者，是你需要一个理智的第二意见时会打电话找的朋友。他们有一种安静的幽默感和强烈的道德感，希望在世上真正有用。忠诚而稳定，他们通过小而一贯的服务之举来表达爱。",
 "The same eye that spots what could be improved can become critical, of others but especially of the self. Virgo people may fret over small details, replay conversations, or struggle to relax until everything is in order, which can make rest feel like something to be earned. Perfectionism can lead to procrastination when a task feels impossible to do well enough. Some Virgo people find it hard to accept help, preferring to be the helper, and may quietly feel taken for granted. Unsolicited advice, though kindly meant, can land as judgement. The constructive path is to practise good enough, to soften the inner critic, and to let others care for them in return.": "那双能发现可改进之处的眼睛，也可能变得挑剔，对别人如此，尤其对自己。处女座的人可能为小细节烦恼，反复回想对话，或者在一切井井有条之前很难放松，这可能让休息感觉像需要挣来的东西。当一项任务感觉不可能做得足够好时，完美主义可能导致拖延。有些处女座的人很难接受帮助，更喜欢当那个帮忙的人，可能会暗暗觉得自己被视为理所当然。不请自来的建议，尽管出于好意，可能听起来像评判。建设性的道路是练习“足够好”，柔化内在的批评者，并让别人也照顾他们。",
 "Virgo people tend to be careful in love, preferring to get to know someone properly before opening up. They may seem reserved at first, but beneath the composure is a deeply caring heart and often a surprisingly earthy sensuality. A Virgo partner shows love in practical ways: remembering what you need, fixing what is broken, planning the details so that your life runs a little more easily. They value honesty, reliability and kindness more than grand gestures, and they notice whether words and actions match. Criticism is sometimes their awkward way of caring, which a partner may need to point out gently. The growth edge in love is letting themselves be adored without needing to earn it, relaxing their standards for the relationship's imperfect, human moments, and saying the tender words aloud rather than only acting them out through service.": "处女座的人在爱情中往往很谨慎，更喜欢在敞开之前好好了解一个人。一开始他们可能显得拘谨，但在沉着之下是一颗深深关怀的心，常常还有一种出人意料的、朴实的感性。处女座的伴侣以实际的方式表达爱：记得你需要什么，修好坏掉的东西，安排好细节让你的生活运转得更轻松一点。他们看重诚实、可靠和善意，胜过宏大的举动，他们也会注意言行是否一致。批评有时是他们笨拙的关心方式，伴侣可能需要温和地指出这一点。爱情中的成长课题是允许自己被爱慕而不必先去挣得，在关系中那些不完美的、人性化的时刻放宽标准，并把温柔的话大声说出来，而不只是通过服务来表现。",
 "Virgo people are often the quiet engine of any workplace. They excel in roles where precision, analysis and service matter: editing, research, accounting, data, science, administration, project management, crafts, teaching and any job that improves how things function. They are thorough, dependable and quick to spot errors before they become problems. Many enjoy learning a skill deeply and refining it over years. They work best with clear standards, the time to do things properly and a sense that their work is genuinely useful. Chaotic environments, or bosses who reward flash over substance, can frustrate them. Virgo people benefit from learning to delegate, to speak up about their contributions more visibly, and to accept that not every task needs to be perfect to be valuable.": "处女座的人常常是任何工作场所里安静的引擎。他们在精确、分析和服务很重要的角色中表现出色：编辑、研究、会计、数据、科学、行政、项目管理、手工艺、教学，以及任何改进事物运作方式的工作。他们周密、可靠，能在错误变成问题之前迅速发现它们。许多人喜欢深入学习一项技能，并用多年时间去打磨它。他们在有清晰标准、有时间好好做事、并感到自己的工作真正有用时工作得最好。混乱的环境，或者奖励华而不实而不是实质的上司，可能让他们沮丧。处女座的人会从学会授权、更显眼地说出自己的贡献、接受并非每项任务都必须完美才有价值中受益。",
 "Virgo self-care often begins with order and simplicity. A tidy space, a fresh notebook, a gentle routine of morning tea and quiet reflection can calm a busy mind. Time in nature, especially gardening or walking among fields and trees, helps Virgo soften and breathe. It is worth practising doing something purely for pleasure, without trying to improve it. Try a small evening ritual: write down three things that went well today, however small, and let that list be enough.": "处女座的自我照顾常常从秩序和简单开始。一个整洁的空间、一本崭新的笔记本、一套早晨喝茶和安静反思的温和日常，都能让忙碌的头脑平静下来。在大自然中的时光，尤其是园艺或在田野和树林间散步，能帮助处女座柔软下来、喘口气。值得练习纯粹为了乐趣去做一件事，而不试图改进它。试试一个小小的晚间仪式：写下今天进展顺利的三件事，无论多小，让这张清单就已足够。",
 "Virgo tends to feel comfortable with fellow earth signs, Taurus and Capricorn, who share its practical outlook and appreciation for reliability. Water signs such as Cancer and Scorpio often bring emotional depth and loyalty that Virgo finds reassuring, and Pisces, its opposite sign, can be a tender pairing of practicality and imagination, each softening the other. Fire and air signs may feel impulsive or scattered to Virgo, yet they can encourage spontaneity and lightness. With patience and respect for each other's way of doing things, any match can flourish.": "处女座往往与同为土象的金牛座和摩羯座感到自在，它们共享处女座务实的眼光和对可靠的欣赏。巨蟹座和天蝎座这样的水象星座常常带来让处女座安心的情感深度与忠诚，作为对宫星座的双鱼座，可以是务实与想象之间一段温柔的组合，彼此柔化对方。火象和风象星座可能让处女座觉得冲动或分散，但它们能鼓励随性和轻松。只要有耐心，尊重彼此做事的方式，任何组合都能兴旺。"
}
